        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Bayeux Tapestry</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1070 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">Probably commissioned by Bishop Odo of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayeux">Bayeux</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a>'s half-brother; most scholars think it was designed and stitched in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, perhaps at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a>, most probably by women needleworkers; French legend credited Queen Matilda</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Form</span><span class="info-stat-val">An embroidery, not a true tapestry: wool thread on a linen ground 68.38 m long and 70 cm tall, in nine sewn panels, 58 scenes with Medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> tituli; the final scenes are missing</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where it is now</span><span class="info-stat-val">Normally the Bayeux Tapestry Museum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayeux">Bayeux</a>, Normandy; on loan to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-museum">British Museum</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> from September 2026 to July 2027</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hastings">Battle of Hastings</a> in 1066; Harold's oath to William; the figure with an arrow in the eye; the earliest known picture of Halley's Comet; a record of 11th-century arms, dress and ships; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/memory-of-the-world-programme">Memory of the World Register</a></span></div>
